Semi-Joins with IN and Anti-Joins with NOT IN
A semi-join is a subquery on another object in an IN clause to restrict the records returned. 
An anti-join is a subquery on another object in a NOT IN clause to restrict the records returned. 
You can create more complex queries by replacing the list of values in the IN or NOT IN clause with a subquery. The subquery can filter by ID (primary key) or reference (foreign key) fields.

The following objects aren’t currently supported in subqueries:
ActivityHistory
Attachments
Event
Note
OpenActivity
Tags (AccountTag, ContactTag, and all other tag objects)
Task
