convertCurrency()

Use convertCurrency() in the SELECT statement of a SOQL query to convert currency fields to the user’s currency. 
This action requires that the org has multiple currencies enabled.

SELECT Id, FORMAT(convertCurrency(AnnualRevenue))
FROM Account


To format currencies according to the user’s locale, use FORMAT() with SELECT() statements.
 In this example, convertedCurrency is an alias for the returned amount, which is formatted appropriately in the user interface.
SELECT Amount, FORMAT(amount) Amt, convertCurrency(amount) convertedAmount,
FORMAT(convertCurrency(amount)) convertedCurrency FROM Opportunity where id = '006R00000024gDtIAI'

SELECT Name, MAX(Amount)
FROM Opportunity
GROUP BY Name
HAVING MAX(Amount) > 10000

